  The spec carries one thing worth your attention beyond what we discussed in chat: the [1mSecurity Posture[0m section states
  plainly that the stored identity is self-asserted client state, that any XSS on the origin can read it, and that a
  shared machine leaks the previous user's attribution until logout. That's the accepted cost of [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m, and it's
  written down so a future change that tries to gate on this value has to argue with the spec first.

  Please review it and let me know if you want changes before I write the implementation plan.

